                            <comment id="15020792" author="githubbot" created="Sun, 22 Nov 2015 01:47:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user asfgit closed the pull request at:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/446&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/446&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15032664" author="jjkeon" created="Mon, 30 Nov 2015 22:57:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Is it possible to patch this for Zeppelin 0.5.5? As a Spark 1.5.2 user who doesn&apos;t not want to rebuild Zeppelin or use a pre-released version, it doesn&apos;t appear there is an option to use a support Zeppelin version until 0.6.0 is released (which likely won&apos;t be soon? Thanks.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15032686" author="jonathak" created="Mon, 30 Nov 2015 23:07:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jjkeon&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jjkeon&quot;&gt;jjkeon&lt;/a&gt;, I don&apos;t know if you happen to be using Zeppelin on Amazon EMR, but if so (or if anybody else using EMR is wondering the same), for emr-4.2.0, which included Spark 1.5.2 and Zeppelin 0.5.5-amzn-0, we backported &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-409&quot; title=&quot;Upgrade to spark 1.5.2&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-409&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-409&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; onto Zeppelin 0.5.5 so that emr-4.2.0 would be able to upgrade to Spark 1.5.2 and still use Zeppelin 0.5.5. (This is why we added the &quot;-amzn-0&quot; suffix to the Zeppelin version; it&apos;s our own custom rolled version of Zeppelin that includes the backport of &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-409&quot; title=&quot;Upgrade to spark 1.5.2&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-409&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-409&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, so we didn&apos;t want to mislead by still calling it simply &quot;0.5.5&quot;.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Similarly, if Zeppelin 0.6.0 has not yet been released by the time EMR upgrades to Spark 1.6, we will likely also backport &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-441&quot; title=&quot;SparkInterpreter does not work if target spark version is not listed in SparkVersion.java &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-441&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-441&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; to Zeppelin 0.5.5 (calling the new version &quot;0.5.5-amzn-1&quot;) in order to allow Zeppelin 0.5.5 to work with Spark 1.6+.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15032713" author="jjkeon" created="Mon, 30 Nov 2015 23:28:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jonathak&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jonathak&quot;&gt;jonathak&lt;/a&gt;, thanks for that information. I&apos;m not using Amazon but the solution you went with seems like something that could easily be generalized for 0.5.5 to allow it to work on Spark 1.5.2.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
